Contract: in an update request, `Tags == nil` means leave existing tags unchanged, while a non-nil empty slice means clear all tags. `NormalizeUpdate` may sort provided tags but must preserve that distinction. The implementation is:

```go
type Update struct {
    Tags []string
}

func NormalizeUpdate(u Update) Update {
    if u.Tags == nil {
        u.Tags = []string{}
    }
    sort.Strings(u.Tags)
    return u
}
```

Does this meet the contract? If not, name the bug and give the minimal fix.
